  "name": "Example: Determining Concave Up and Concave Down Curves",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029011/assets/f8377fe3d48db6f576ac6534d435b06baae510dd66c239782705c51f06fb7ec5.png)\n\nWhich of the curves above are concave up?",
  "worked_solution": "The concavity of a function refers to the direction in which its graph curves.\n\n- If the graph curves upward, like a \"smile\" ($\\smile$), then the graph is said to be *concave up*.\n\n- If the graph curves downward, like a \"frown\" ($\\frown$), then the graph is said to be *concave down*.\n\nIt's helpful to remember the mnemonic \"concave down like a frown.\"\n\nOnly graph II curves upward (like a \"smile\") among the given graphs.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-e10002\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Determining Concave Up and Concave Down Curves</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e10002\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <div id=\"graphic-8492ba35b1e03c9d202786434dd3bec0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/8492ba35b1e03c9d202786434dd3bec0\"></div>\n\n<p>Which of the curves above are concave up?</p>\n\n                    </div>     \n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>The concavity of a function refers to the direction in which its graph curves.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>If the graph curves upward, like a \"smile\" (<span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.324ex\" height=\"1.343ex\" style=\"vertical-align: 0.309ex; margin-bottom: -0.48ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -504.3 1000.5 578.1\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\\smile</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E1-MJMAIN-2323\" d=\"M923 378Q944 378 944 358Q944 345 912 311T859 259Q710 134 500 134Q288 134 140 259Q55 336 55 358Q55 366 61 372T75 378Q78 378 84 376Q86 376 101 356T147 310T221 257T339 212T500 193Q628 193 734 236Q841 282 903 363Q914 378 923 378Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-2323\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span>), then the graph is said to be <em>concave up</em>.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>If the graph curves downward, like a \"frown\" (<span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.324ex\" height=\"1.343ex\" style=\"vertical-align: 0.281ex; margin-bottom: -0.452ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -504.3 1000.5 578.1\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\">\\frown</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E2-MJMAIN-2322\" d=\"M55 141Q55 149 72 174T125 234T209 303T329 360T478 388H526Q649 383 765 319Q814 291 858 250T923 179T944 141Q944 133 938 128T924 122Q914 124 912 125T902 139Q766 328 500 328Q415 328 342 308T225 258T150 199T102 148T84 124Q81 122 75 122Q55 127 55 141Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAIN-2322\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span>), then the graph is said to be <em>concave down</em>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It's helpful to remember the mnemonic \"concave down like a frown.\"</p>\n<p>Only graph II curves upward (like a \"smile\") among the given graphs.</p>\n\n                    </div>     \n                </div>                            \n                    \n            </div>",
